Z||000000||BAM-BAM||05-28-2000||11:59 PM||||  Was the 5 speed in the 88 4cyl a getrag? if so what should I pay the guy for the one he has. It looks brand new. If I want it all<BR>I have to do is pull it. TIA for any advice.<P> Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||GWMORGAN||05-29-2000||12:11 AM||||The 88 4cyls. all came with the Isuzu 5spd. tranny.||||reg||1
Z||000002||cobra427||05-29-2000||12:34 AM||||Bam,<BR>Just for added info, the 85-88 5 sp MT2 was the Isuzu. <BR>The 86-88 5 sp MG2 was the Muncie.<BR>All other transmissions were the Muncie (4 sp) MY8,M17,M19||||reg||1
Z||000003||BAM-BAM||05-29-2000||09:25 AM||||    What would be a good price for a non Getrag 5 speed? He wants $300.00 for the one he has. All I have to do is pull it. The car has 67,000 miles and was hit from the rear, not really bad either. If it wasn't already picked over I would buy the whole damn thing.<BR> Is an Isuzu or Muncie worth that much?<P>Thnx, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000004||GWMORGAN||05-29-2000||12:45 PM||||I paid $150.00 for my 87 Isuzu tranny with 70k miles on it. The junk-yard man also threw in the shifter and cables for free and I didn't have to pull it myself.<BR>IMHO, I think yours a bit pricy.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||GWMORGAN||05-29-2000||12:46 PM||||I paid $150.00 for my 87 Isuzu tranny with 70k miles on it. The junk-yard man also threw in the shifter and cables for free and I didn't have to pull it myself.<BR>IMHO, I think yours a bit pricy.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||SCCA FIERO||05-29-2000||04:36 PM||||I paid $150 for an 88 Isuzu with the shifter, slave, cables, rear struts, rear calipers and rotors, trailing arms and lateral links. I got a very good deal, but I wouldn't go over $150 for a good used Isuzu, even if all you get is the tranny.||||reg||1
Z||000007||MikeE||06-01-2000||05:47 AM||||I actually gave away the Isuzu 5sp that I had  after I pulled all the parts I needed from my parts car but Fieros are very cheap here so I probably couldn't have sold it anyway.  I had a hard time giving it away.  The person was supposed to take the whole car but when I went to check on it I found it on blocks with the trans & rear axles missing.  That's what I get for trying to be nice.<P>By the way, what Cobra427 was really saying was that the so-called Getrag 5sp is actually a Muncie 282. Getrag never made a trans for the Fiero, rather Muncie manufactured it using a Getrag design but people (and even some manuals) commonly refer to it as the Getrag, perhaps to avoid any confusion between the 4 & 5 speeds but more likely out of some inate believe that Getrag makes a better trans (not always true). This erroneous labeling could lead to problems when looking for parts because Getrag did make a trans labeled 282 but it was for another car (non-GM) and it was longitudinal.  This info came from someone on another list who was looking for parts for the Getrag 284 used with the 3.4 DOHC V6 which was a Getrag, so he called Getrag directly.  However, by an agreement with GM they do not make any replacement parts (GM used to sell parts but no cases-they want to sell the whole trans).  Therefore, he also asked about the Getrag 282 from the Fiero since 3.4 owners often use it for a replacement when their 284 goes south (a common occurance-the trans is too weak for the engine).  They had never heard of the trans and thought he might be talking about the 282 they did make although they assured him that it wasn't for a GM car.  However, GM does still make parts for this trans so as long as one deals with GM and not Getrag there will not be a problem.<P>[This message has been edited by MikeE (edited 06-01-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by MikeE (edited 06-01-2000).]||||reg||1
